export const TEMPLATE11_MANDATE_TEXT: string = "# Strategy #11 Mandate — Polydash Momentum Fund\n\nStrategy #11 is published on the live StrategyTemplate contract\n(`0xb2a958a9779e02764de006c8aeebc36174e2e3ba`) and is readable by the\nV2 tokenized fund factory. The mandate text below is the\ntemplate's `mandateUri` document (to be pinned to IPFS; the published\n`mandateUri` is the resulting `ipfs://` CID).\n\n## Mandate\n\n> The Polydash Momentum Fund buys allowlisted tokens that are rising —\n> tokens with rising prices and rising trading volume — and sells or trims\n> them when that momentum fades or reverses. The manager picks each token\n> in public: every new token is proposed with a written thesis, waits\n> 2 days in public, and anyone can leave the tokenized fund during the\n> wait. Buys are executed in small tranches, each no more than 10% of NAV,\n> paced across days, never chasing a vertical spike. No single token may\n> ever be more than 30% of the tokenized fund. Un-deployed ETH stays in\n> WETH in the vault, visible on the public NAV tape. The manager's\n> performance fee is 5% of new gains above the high-water mark only.\n> No leverage, no shorting, no assets outside the allowlist.\n\n## Template parameters (as published)\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Assets | `[]` (no fixed assets — the manager proposes allowlisted tokens, each with a 2-day public wait; WETH is the quote asset and is always in the mandate implicitly) |\n| Max position | 3000 bps (30% of NAV in any one token — the standard per-asset cap) |\n| Max trade | 1000 bps (10% of NAV per trade) |\n| Max deviation | 500 bps (5% vs TWAP feed) |\n| HWM performance fee | 500 bps (5% of new gains only) |\n| Max drawdown | 2000 bps (20% NAV drop pauses new buys) |\n| Skin lock | 2592000 s (30 days) |\n\n## Momentum rules\n\n- Momentum means a token whose price and trading volume are both rising over recent days. The manager writes down, in the proposal thesis, what momentum they see and why they expect it to continue.\n- Never chase a vertical spike: a token that has already spiked sharply is not bought until it settles. Trades are refused if the price is more than 5% away from the time-weighted average price (TWAP).\n- Trim or sell when momentum fades: falling volume, a broken rising trend, or a thesis that no longer holds. The manager does not hold a fading token hoping it comes back.\n- Only tokens on the approved list (the allowlist) can ever be bought. Every new token waits 2 days in public before the manager can add it.\n- No leverage, no shorting. The fund only buys tokens it holds.\n\n## Fund terms (Season 1, as proposed — confirm before creating the fund)\n\n- Mint price 0.01 ETH, raise cap 2 ETH (200 shares), manager skin 5%\n  (10 shares, 0.1 ETH) bought before public mint, entry fee 0%.\n- Exits in-kind (pro-rata holdings + WETH).\n\n## Publish checklist\n\n- [ ] Pin this document to IPFS; record the CID as `mandateUri`.\n- [ ] `publish(mandateHash, mandateUri, [], 3000, 1000, 500, 500, 2000, 2592000)` on StrategyTemplate (owner tx — needs the deployer key).\n- [ ] Verify `templateCount` incremented to 11 and `getTemplate(11)` reads back the params above.\n- [ ] Add Strategy #11 to the create flow (V2 factory routing + name) so it appears as a choice.\n";
